WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.325
So here's the ask.

2
00:00:01.325 --> 00:00:04.150
Approve a small pilot in
a developer instance.

3
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.500
Made-up data only.

4
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.763
One or two staff, trained
on the rules first.

5
00:00:08.763 --> 00:00:12.975
An approved AI tool, and a named
reviewer who isn't the author.

6
00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:16.175
And one component: the check
that refuses to close a

7
00:00:16.175 --> 00:00:19.375
piece of work until a fresh
read proves the fix held.

8
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:22.800
The code goes into an agency
repository from day one.

9
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.769
At the end of the pilot, we come back
with the code, the test results,

10
00:00:26.769 --> 00:00:30.438
the review records, and an honest
list of what failed review.

11
00:00:30.438 --> 00:00:34.788
Then you decide whether it moves to our
test instance, through a normal change.

12
00:00:34.788 --> 00:00:37.807
It's small, it's reversible,
it needs no new money,

13
00:00:37.807 --> 00:00:41.760
and it shows you the evidence
before anyone commits to more.
